   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Unreal parole present",
   "texto": [
    "It is used for something that is not real now: **Wenn ich mehr Zeit hätte, würde ich Sport machen** (if I had more time, I would do sport). The sentence with «wenn» carries the verb in Konjunktiv II at the end; the main one starts with **würde** + infinitive.",
    "With **sein**, **haben** and the manners are used directly the Konjunktiv II: **wäre** (would), **hätte** (would), **könnte** (could). They're the most common ways."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Forms of Konjunktiv II",
   "texto": [
    "Some common forms are based on Präteritum and can carry diéresis: **kommen → käme**, **gehen → ginge**, **wissen → wüsste**. Not all verbs change the vocal; with many it is used **würde + infinitivo**. The Konjunktiv II expresses hypothesis or courtesy, not «when»."
   ]
